# J96 GPU: GPC 1 power-state dump, 2026-11-09 ~21:05 GMT, boot 9484673f (fresh j96-boot)
# Kernel 7.3.0-rc1-j96-firstboot+ (the dev-image/artifacts build; config hash matches artifacts/kernel.config).
# Module gpu/probe/apple-j96-gpudump.ko sha256 e83a8079...c5f0a4, loaded after unbinding the built-in
# apple-j96-gpuprobe. No RGX access. Desktop stopped, tty1 console in front. Slow token first, then the
# timed token, same boot. Both finished (result=0); the iPad stayed up.
#
# Findings:
# - All seven Fender registers are readable while ps_gfx is on, at GPC 0 and at GPC 1 (first time read).
# - Powered, before any write (dump A, both runs): every Fender register reads 0. The second run's dump A
#   is all-zero again, so Fender state does not survive a ps_gfx off/on cycle.
# - At GPC 1 nothing changes from +0 us to +1 s (dumps B-F identical): sleep=0x40000000 (as written),
#   perf=0x1, intst=0x2 (one unacked Fender interrupt bit raised by the 0->1 transition), kick=0, next=0,
#   ovr=0, ps_gfx=0x3ff (target 0xf, actual 0xf, was-gated flags set).
# - After GPC 0 (dump G): perf=0, intst=0x3 (bit 0 added by the 1->0 transition), sleep still 0x40000000.
# - So at the moment stage 4 read RGX+0x20 and froze, Fender and ps_gfx already show their final state,
#   and waiting up to 1 s changes nothing they report. A longer delay alone is unlikely to fix the RGX read;
#   whatever keeps the RGX CR window from answering is not visible in these eight registers.
#
